---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Sidebar from "../components/Sidebar.astro";
import { getHeroById } from "../data/heroes";

const RECOMMENDED_COMPS = [
  {
    label: "PVE — Sustain + Energy Lock",
    heroes: ["nuba", "nezha", "demeter", "freya", "pan"],
    reason: "Nuba's Doom Mark pressure pairs with Pan and Demeter's Energy drain, while Freya stabilizes long fights and Nezha provides a reliable DPS anchor.",
    notes: [
      "Freya's team healing can keep Nuba alive long enough to build revive sources.",
      "Nezha brings consistent front-loaded damage to cover Nuba's lower burst output."
    ]
  },
  {
    label: "PVP — Control + Bruiser Core",
    heroes: ["nuba", "hladgunnr", "jormungandr", "wenshen", "pan"],
    reason: "Nuba's ATK SPD drain stacks with Wen-Shen's ATK down and control procs, while Jormungandr soaks burst and punishes focus to open windows for Hladgunnr's damage.",
    notes: [
      "Pan's silence and daze can delay enemy ultimates, amplifying Nuba's Energy destruction.",
      "Jormungandr's Revenge window turns enemy burst into lethal counter-damage."
    ]
  }
];

function heroName(id) {
  const hero = getHeroById(id);
  if (hero?.name) return hero.name;
  return `${id.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}${id.slice(1)}`;
}

function heroImage(id) {
  const hero = getHeroById(id);
  const img = hero?.image || `/heroes/${id}.webp`;
  return img.startsWith("/") ? img : `/${img}`;
}
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Nuba – Goddess of Drought | Hero Guide</title>
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/html2pdf.js/0.10.1/html2pdf.bundle.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<Sidebar />

<div class="container">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <header class="hero-header">
    <div class="epithet">Motto Immortal · Hero Guide</div>
    <img class="hero-portrait" src="/img_data/nubaFace.webp" alt="Nuba portrait" loading="lazy" />
    <h1 class="hero-name">Nuba</h1>
    <p class="hero-quote">"The world fears, banishes, and curses me. But I just don't understand what I've done wrong."</p>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag tag-faction">
        <img src="/icons/factions/clubs.webp" alt="Club Faction" class="tag-icon" />
        Clubs Faction
      </span>
      <span class="tag tag-class">
        <img src="/icons/classes/warrior.webp" alt="Warrior Class" class="tag-icon" />
        Warrior
      </span>
      <button id="downloadPdfBtn" class="tag tag-download">⇓ Download as PDF</button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- JUMP NAVIGATION -->
  <nav class="jump-nav">
    <div class="jump-nav-title">Quick Navigation</div>
    <div class="jump-nav-links">
      <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
      <a href="#faction-synergy">Faction Synergy</a>
      <a href="#doom-mechanic">Doom Mark</a>
      <a href="#skills">Skills</a>
      <a href="#ratings">Ratings</a>
      <a href="#positioning">Positioning</a>
      <a href="#comps">Comps</a>
      <a href="#strengths">Strengths</a>
      <a href="#synergy">Synergy</a>
      <a href="#playstyle">Playstyle</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <section class="section" id="overview">
    <div class="section-title">Overview</div>
    <div class="overview-card">
      <p>Nuba, the <em>Goddess of Drought</em>, appears to be a <strong>Warrior</strong> of the <strong>Club</strong> faction whose entire kit revolves around a unique debuff called <doom>Crimson Doom Mark</doom>. She appears to be a sustained-pressure hybrid — part debuffer, part disabler, part self-sustaining frontliner — who could work by marking enemies, draining their resources, and punishing them for carrying her mark.</p>
      <p>Unlike most Warriors who deal straightforward burst damage, Nuba could layer multiple stacking debuffs over time while simultaneously reducing enemy effectiveness and amplifying her own follow-up damage. Her passive resurrection mechanic via <em>Rise of the Drought</em> could give her unexpected survivability in extended fights.</p>
      <p>As a Club faction hero, Nuba could scale strongly when fielded alongside other Club heroes — the faction bonus grants stacking ATK and HP to the whole team, potentially reinforcing a durable front-row role.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FACTION SYNERGY -->
  <section class="section" id="faction-synergy">
    <div class="section-title">Club Faction Synergy</div>
    <div class="mechanic-box" style="border-color: rgba(64,106,95,0.35); background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(64,106,95,0.07), rgba(64,106,95,0.05));">
      <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">Faction Bonus — Club</div>
      <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px;">Fielding multiple Club faction heroes grants the <em>entire team</em> bonus ATK and HP. Thresholds:</p>
      <ul class="mechanic-list">
        <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">3 Club heroes:</strong> +15% ATK &amp; HP for the team</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">3 + 2 (mixed):</strong> +25% ATK &amp; HP for the team</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">4 Club heroes:</strong> +30% ATK &amp; HP for the team</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">5 Club heroes:</strong> +35% ATK &amp; HP for the team — maximum bonus</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:14px; font-style:italic;">Based on skill mechanics, Nuba could benefit from sustained HP (enabling her revive to matter more) and amplified ATK (making her Stun windows hit harder). Maximizing the Club faction count could strengthen her kit. Even hitting the 3-hero threshold for +15% could be a meaningful upgrade — running 4–5 Club heroes could be a viable dedicated archetype around her.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CRIMSON DOOM MARK -->
  <section class="section" id="doom-mechanic">
    <div class="section-title">Core Mechanic — Crimson Doom Mark</div>
    <div class="mechanic-box">
      <div class="mechanic-label">The Doom Mark System</div>
      <ul class="mechanic-list">
        <li>Applied to enemies at the <strong>start of battle</strong> passively via her Ultimate passive, and re-applied to the nearest enemy whenever the Ultimate activates.</li>
        <li>Marked enemies <strong>deal reduced damage</strong> — confirmed by both Curse of Decay and Rite of Ashes.</li>
        <li>When a Doom Mark expires naturally ("falls"), it drains the target's essence and spawns a <strong>Source of the Drought Devil</strong> at the target's location.</li>
        <li>Every time Nuba casts her Ultimate, all marked enemies <strong>permanently lose ATK SPD</strong> — this effect stacks with each Ultimate cast.</li>
        <li>Skill 1 (Infernal Soulbreaker) deals bonus damage and <strong>Stuns</strong> targets that carry the mark.</li>
        <li>The Source of the Drought Devil serves as a <strong>revive token</strong> — consumed by Rise of the Drought to bring Nuba back to life at her current position.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SKILLS -->
  <section class="section" id="skills">
    <div class="section-title">Skill Breakdown</div>
    <div class="skills-grid">

      <div class="skill-card ultimate">
        <div class="skill-header">
          <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/nuba_ultimate.png" alt="Siphon of Souls" />
          <span class="skill-name">Siphon of Souls</span>
          <span class="skill-badge badge-ultimate">Ultimate</span>
        </div>
        <p class="skill-desc">
          <strong>Passive component:</strong> At the start of battle, inflicts <doom>Crimson Doom Mark</doom> on enemies, dealing damage to the host and destroying their Energy. When a Doom Mark expires, it drains the target's essence and transforms into a <em>Source of the Drought Devil</em> at the target's location.<br><br>
          <strong>Active component:</strong> Upon activation, inflicts <doom>Crimson Doom Mark</doom> on the nearest enemy, <highlight>disabling them</highlight>, dealing damage, and absorbing their Energy.
        </p>
        <div class="skill-note">
          Dual-purpose: passive mark spread at battle start + active single-target mark, disable, and Energy drain. <strong>Energy context:</strong> all heroes fill their Energy bar passively at the start of a fight — when full, the Ultimate fires automatically. Nuba's Ultimate both <em>destroys</em> enemy Energy (potentially resetting or delaying their next cast) and <em>absorbs</em> it (potentially accelerating her own refill). This could delay how fast enemies can cast their own Ultimates. Other heroes, items, or skills can speed up or slow down Energy fill rate — if so, Nuba's drain could compound any existing slow-fill debuffs on enemies.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="skill-card relic">
        <div class="skill-header">
          <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/nuba_relic.png" alt="Curse of Decay" />
          <span class="skill-name">Curse of Decay</span>
          <span class="skill-badge badge-relic">Relic</span>
        </div>
        <p class="skill-desc">
          Enemies infested with <doom>Crimson Doom Mark</doom> deal less DMG. Each time Nuba casts her Ultimate, all enemies infested with Crimson Doom Mark <highlight>permanently lose ATK SPD</highlight>.
        </p>
        <div class="skill-note">
          Relic passive — would be active once unlocked. If the mechanics work as described, the ATK SPD reduction could stack across every Ultimate cast. Based on available information this reduction does not appear to have diminishing returns, meaning repeated Ultimate casts could theoretically reduce enemy attack speed significantly in longer fights. If so, she could become exponentially more dangerous as she fills her Energy more often.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="skill-header">
          <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/nuba_skill_1.png" alt="Infernal Soulbreaker" />
          <span class="skill-name">Infernal Soulbreaker</span>
          <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 1</span>
        </div>
        <p class="skill-desc">
          Deal damage to an enemy and <highlight>interrupt</highlight> them. If the target has <doom>Crimson Doom Mark</doom>, the skill deals higher damage and <highlight>Stuns</highlight> the target instead of simply interrupting.
        </p>
        <div class="skill-note">
          Could be a primary CC tool. Would need a marked target to reach full potential — which appears likely in most fights thanks to her Ultimate passive. If the Stun is reliable, this could be excellent for both PVE bosses and PVP targets.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="skill-header">
          <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/nuba_skill_2.png" alt="Rise of the Drought" />
          <span class="skill-name">Rise of the Drought</span>
          <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 2</span>
        </div>
        <p class="skill-desc">
          <strong>Lv4:</strong> When Nuba falls in battle, she consumes one <em>Source of the Drought Devil</em> to revive at her current location and restore HP.
        </p>
        <div class="skill-note">
          Self-revive gated behind the Drought Devil sources generated by expiring Doom Marks. Requires investment to Lv4 to activate. Strategy would involve early mark application to build up revive sources for later in the fight.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="skill-card relic">
        <div class="skill-header">
          <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/nuba_skill_3.png" alt="Rite of Ashes" />
          <span class="skill-name">Rite of Ashes</span>
          <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 3</span>
        </div>
        <p class="skill-desc">
          Enemies infested with <doom>Crimson Doom Mark</doom> deal less DMG. Each time Nuba casts her Ultimate, all enemies infested with Crimson Doom Mark <highlight>permanently lose ATK SPD</highlight>.
        </p>
        <div class="skill-note">
          Shares its description with Curse of Decay — likely compounds the same debuff stack, effectively doubling the ATK SPD reduction and DMG reduction layers per Ultimate cast, or grants an additional independent stack.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RATINGS -->
  <section class="section" id="ratings">
    <div class="section-title">Potential Mode Ratings</div>
    <div class="rating-grid">
      <div class="rating-card">
        <div class="rating-mode">PVP</div>
      <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge rating-s">S</span></div>
        <div class="rating-desc">CC + ATK SPD drain = oppressive in front row</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rating-card">
        <div class="rating-mode">Campaign / PVE</div>
        <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge rating-a">A</span></div>
        <div class="rating-desc">Solid debuffer; revive adds longevity</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rating-card">
        <div class="rating-mode">Boss Fights</div>
        <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge rating-b">B</span></div>
        <div class="rating-desc">Energy drain slows boss ults; Stun useful</div>
      </div>

                 
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:12px; font-style:italic; text-align:center;">* Ratings based solely on skill analysis. No external tier list data used.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- POSITIONING -->
  <section class="section" id="positioning">
    <div class="section-title">Recommended Positioning</div>
    <div class="pos-grid">
      <div class="pos-card">
        <div class="pos-mode">PVP — Front Row</div>
        <p>Nuba could be positioned in the <strong>front row</strong> of PVP compositions. Her ATK SPD drain could stack up while enemies chip away at her, and her self-revive from Drought Devil sources could provide exceptional staying power during opening phases. If executed properly, she could potentially shred enemy attack speed and remain fighting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pos-card">
        <div class="pos-mode">PVE — Front or Mid</div>
        <p>In PVE (campaign, bosses), Nuba could potentially anchor the front line while her marks generate Drought Devil sources for the revive. Her Energy drain on the Ultimate active may delay boss ultimate activations, buying time for backline DPS to scale. She could function as a <strong>utility frontliner</strong> rather than a primary carry.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RECOMMENDED COMPS -->
  <section class="section" id="comps">
    <div class="section-title">Suggested Comps</div>
    <div class="comp-list">
      {RECOMMENDED_COMPS.map(comp => (
        <div class="comp-entry">
          <div class="comp-entry-header">
            <span class="comp-label">{comp.label}</span>
            <p class="comp-reason">{comp.reason}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="comp-hero-row">
            {comp.heroes.map(id => (
              <a href={`/heroes/${id}`} class="hero-chip">
                <img src={heroImage(id)} alt={heroName(id)} loading="lazy" />
                <span class="hero-chip-name">{heroName(id)}</span>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
          {comp.notes?.length > 0 && (
            <ul class="comp-notes">
              {comp.notes.map(n => <li>{n}</li>)}
            </ul>
          )}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STRENGTHS / WEAKNESSES -->
  <section class="section" id="strengths">
    <div class="section-title">Strengths &amp; Weaknesses</div>
    <div class="sw-grid">
      <div class="sw-card strengths">
        <div class="sw-title">Theoretical Strengths</div>
        <ul class="sw-list">
          <li>Could apply <doom>Crimson Doom Mark</doom> at battle start — potentially no ramp-up required for debuffing</li>
          <li>Stacking ATK SPD reduction on marked enemies could make her more dangerous the longer a fight lasts</li>
          <li>Built-in self-revive through Drought Devil sources could provide exceptional staying power</li>
          <li>Energy drain/destruction on Ultimate could delay and disrupt enemy ultimate rotations</li>
          <li>Could enable reliable Stun on Skill 1 against marked targets — potentially near-100% CC uptime</li>
          <li>Interrupt on Skill 1 even without marks could provide baseline disruption</li>
          <li>Potential dual debuff coverage: DMG reduction + ATK SPD reduction simultaneously</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="sw-card weaknesses">
        <div class="sw-title">Theoretical Weaknesses</div>
        <ul class="sw-list">
          <li>Self-revive requires Skill 2 at Lv4 — would be non-functional at lower investment</li>
          <li>Revive depends on Drought Devil sources existing — if marks expire before she dies, she may have no revive available</li>
          <li>Single-target focus on Ultimate active — mark re-application would hit only <em>nearest</em> enemy</li>
          <li>No direct healing outside of the revive HP restore — could be vulnerable to sustained burst before marks expire</li>
          <li>Utility-focused — may not function as a standalone damage carry; could need supporting DPS in the backline</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SYNERGY -->
  <section class="section" id="synergy">
    <div class="section-title">Synergy Considerations</div>
    <div class="synergy-note">
      <p><strong>Club faction stacking</strong> could be Nuba's most concrete synergy path. Running 3–5 Club heroes would give the whole team bonus ATK and HP — both stats could benefit Nuba (more HP could extend her revive window; more ATK could amplify her Stun damage). A full 5-Club composition would give +35% to the entire lineup, potentially making it a viable dedicated archetype around her.</p>
      <br>
      <p>Mechanically, Nuba could pair well with <strong>heroes that slow enemy Energy fill rate</strong> — since her Ultimate destroys enemy Energy, any hero that further delays enemies reaching their Ultimate could create a compounding effect where enemy ultimates fire less frequently. Similarly, heroes that <strong>speed up Nuba's own Energy fill</strong> could let her cast her Ultimate more often, stacking ATK SPD reductions faster.</p>
      <br>
      <p>In PVP, she could potentially benefit from a <strong>second frontliner</strong> who can absorb pressure while her ATK SPD stacks accumulate — ideally another Club Warrior or tank. Backline <strong>scaling DPS heroes</strong> could synergize well since Nuba's debuffs could buy them the time they need to scale their damage.</p>
      <br>
      <p><strong>Note:</strong> Specific hero names for synergy require knowing the full roster and in-game testing. The above is based purely on mechanical and faction synergy logic from skill data.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider-ornament">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

  <!-- PLAYSTYLE SUMMARY -->
  <section class="section" id="playstyle">
    <div class="section-title">Playstyle Summary</div>
    <div class="overview-card">
      <p>Nuba appears to be a <em>slow-burn oppressor</em> — theoretically, she would not win fights instantly, but rather by making enemies progressively less capable of fighting back. Based on skill mechanics, every Ultimate cast could tax the enemy team's speed and damage, every Skill 1 could be a near-guaranteed Stun, and every expiring Doom Mark could feed her revive pool.</p>
      <p>She could be at her best in <strong>prolonged PVP engagements</strong> where her stacking debuffs compound, and could potentially function as a <strong>frontline disruptor</strong> in PVE where her Energy drain disrupts boss timing. She requires investment (especially Skill 2 to Lv4), and if effective in-game, could reward it with outsized survivability and sustained enemy suppression.</p>
      <p>If she lives up to these mechanics, strategy would involve positioning her in the front row, marking enemies at the start, casting her Ultimate as often as possible to stack the ATK SPD drain, and accumulating Drought Devils as backup revive tokens.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="guide-footer">
    Motto Immortal · Nuba Guide · Based on in-game skill data only · No speculative additions
  </footer>

  <!-- BACK TO TOP BUTTON -->
  <button id="backToTopBtn" class="back-to-top" title="Back to top">↑</button>

</div>

<Footer />

<script>
  // Back to top button functionality
  const backToTopBtn = document.getElementById('backToTopBtn');
  window.addEventListener('scroll', function() {
    if (window.scrollY > 500) {
      backToTopBtn.classList.add('show');
    } else {
      backToTopBtn.classList.remove('show');
    }
  });

  backToTopBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
    window.scrollTo({
      top: 0,
      behavior: 'smooth'
    });
  });

  // PDF download button functionality
  document.getElementById('downloadPdfBtn').addEventListener('click', function() {
    const element = document.querySelector('.container');
    
    // Create a clone for PDF with modified styles
    const clonedElement = element.cloneNode(true);
    const tempContainer = document.createElement('div');
    tempContainer.style.backgroundColor = '#0d0b10';
    tempContainer.style.color = '#E8DDD0';
    tempContainer.style.padding = '20px';
    tempContainer.appendChild(clonedElement);
    
    const opt = {
      margin: 10,
      filename: 'Nuba-Hero-Guide.pdf',
      image: { type: 'jpeg', quality: 0.98 },
      html2canvas: { 
        scale: 2, 
        useCORS: true, 
        logging: false, 
        allowTaint: true,
        backgroundColor: '#0d0b10'
      },
      jsPDF: { orientation: 'portrait', unit: 'mm', format: 'a4' },
      pagebreak: { mode: ['avoid-all', 'css', 'legacy'] }
    };
    
    html2pdf().set(opt).from(tempContainer).save();
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --crimson: #406a5f;
    --crimson-bright: #406a5f;
    --crimson-glow: #406a5f;
    --gold: rgba(250, 204, 21, 0.95);
    --gold-light: rgba(250, 234, 121, 0.95);
    --dark: #0D0A0A;
    --dark-mid: #1A1212;
    --dark-card: #130E0E;
    --text: #E8DDD0;
    --text-muted: #9A8A7A;
    --doom-purple: #406a5f;
    --doom-purple-light: #406a5f;
    --accent-teal: #406a5f;
    --accent-blue: #406a5f;
    --skill-text: #ffffff;
    --skill-bg: #407264;
    
  }

  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    background: 
      linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(13, 10, 10, 0.92) 0%, rgba(7, 6, 12, 0.85) 50%, rgba(7, 6, 12, 0.92) 100%),
      url(/img_data/nuba2-1.webp) center/cover fixed,
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 30% -10%, rgba(64,106,95,0.15), transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 80% 20%, rgba(64,106,95,0.08), transparent 55%),
      linear-gradient(to bottom, #0d0b10, #07060c);
    background-blend-mode: multiply, normal, screen, screen, normal;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: "Spectral", "Roboto", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    min-height: 100vh;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    margin-left: 80px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    body {
      margin-left: 0;
      margin-bottom: 60px;
    }
  }

  /* Atmospheric background overlay */
  body::before {
    content: '';
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 40% at 50% 0%, rgba(64,106,95,0.18) 0%, transparent 70%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 40% 60% at 80% 50%, rgba(64,106,95,0.08) 0%, transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 30% 30% at 20% 80%, rgba(64,106,95,0.1) 0%, transparent 50%);
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px 60px;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  /* ── HERO HEADER ── */
  .hero-header {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 60px 0 40px;
    position: relative;
    page-break-after: avoid;
  }

  .hero-portrait {
    margin-top: px;
    width: 128px;
    height: 128px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin: 0 auto 18px;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid rgba(250, 234, 121, 0.45);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 4px rgb(255, 228, 122),
      0 0 28px rgba(250, 204, 21, 0.32),
      0 0 64px rgba(250, 234, 121, 0.2),
      0 18px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
  }



  .epithet {
    font-family: "Spectral", "Roboto", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.35em;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .hero-name {
    font-family: "Spectral", "Roboto", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(52px, 10vw, 88px);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1;
    text-shadow:
      0 0 40px rgba(130,75,162,0.8),
      0 0 80px rgba(130,75,162,0.4),
      0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.8);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .hero-name span {
    color: var(--crimson-bright);
  }

  .hero-quote {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-muted);
